  "articleBody": "Choosing the right trim can totally transform a room, but with so many options, how do you pick? It really comes down to a few key things. First, think about the overall style of your home. Are you going for a classic, traditional look, or something more modern and sleek? Different trim profiles will complement different aesthetics. You also need to consider how the new trim will blend with any existing millwork, like door and window casings. You don't want it to clash, so matching or finding something complementary is usually the way to go. Don't forget about practicality too! Will your trim include baseboards, casing, or crown molding? Each serves a different purpose and adds a distinct feel. The material choice matters too, whether it's wood, MDF, or something else, impacting durability and how easily it can be finished. Finally, think about the condition of your walls. Older homes often have uneven surfaces, which might require a bit more patching around the new trim to get that perfect, seamless look. If you're unsure about how to integrate new trim with old or have intricate corners, a professional can really help guide your choices and ensure a flawless installation. They can make sure everything lines up perfectly, even with those tricky, uneven walls.",
